# SI dimension algebra for the measurement units (issue #700, E58).
#
# Each `si_unit` record states one unit's dimension as a product of the
# seven SI base dimensions and its factor to the coherent SI unit of that
# dimension, so any two units of the same dimension convert through SI
# even when no pairwise `conversion` record exists in
# data/seed/meanings-units.lino (issue #1176's engine converts stated
# pairs; this table derives the rest).
#
# Base dimension symbols: L length, M mass, T time, I electric current,
# K thermodynamic temperature, N amount of substance, J luminous
# intensity. A `dimension` of `1` is dimensionless. Exponent digits follow
# the symbol (`L2MT-3` is the watt's kg·m²/s³).
#
# `si_factor` is a terminating decimal (exact as written) or an exact
# `num/den` fraction for repeating values (5/18 for km/h). `surface`
# rows are recognition words (plain data, matched lowercase); the units
# that also live in meanings-units.lino keep their full five-language
# lexemes there — this table adds dimensions and factors, not vocabulary.
#
# Read by rust/src/si_units.rs through crate::seed::seed_files().
